extends RefCounted
## Recipes (owner rpg-core). Re-exported as Data.RECIPES; every recipe id is ALSO a dish item id in Data.ITEMS (kind "dish").
## Fields: name, slots (2-3 entries; each an ingredient id, "cheese" = any cheese wheel, or "tag:<tag>" = any ingredient
##   with that tag), pair (cheese id that pairs perfectly: +1 quality tier when used in the cheese slot, or "" ),
##   learn ("start" known at new game | "npc:<npc_id>" taught | "discover" found by experimenting | "quest:<id>"),
##   hint (shown in the recipe book before discovery), effect (same keys as Data.ITEMS consumables, see items.gd),
##   element (for thrown dishes), price (sell value at Plain), desc.
## Matching (Data.match_recipe / DB.match_recipe): order-independent; exact ids beat tags beat "cheese"; extra items fail.
## No match -> "mystery_mush". Quality (DB.QUALITY): burnt 0.5x, plain 1.0x, tasty 1.35x, gourmet 1.75x (+gauge bonus).
## Quality = stir timing result (0..3) + pairing bonus (perfect cheese pair, or all slot flavours distinct = "balanced"),
##   clamped 0..3; cook_role perks in characters.gd adjust it.

